From d897237345283e815808c5139e643e297a3f1ddb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 14:59:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 16/42] transports+configstore: POST
 /api/tenants/{tenant_id}/providers (admin create per-tenant provider)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The minimum-viable patch to provision per-tenant providers via the API
so an E2E harness can boot a tenant, configure its OpenAI/Anthropic/etc
provider, and immediately drive inference against that tenant's runtime.

configstore additions:
- ConfigStore.AddProviderForTenant(ctx, tenantID, provider, config) pins
  tenant_id on the new TableProvider row (and on its TableKey rows) so
  the result is only visible to GetProvidersConfigByTenant(tenantID).
  Empty tenantID normalizes to tables.DefaultTenantID, matching the
  existing GetProvidersConfigByTenant policy.
- Legacy AddProvider now routes through addProviderInternal with
  tenant_id=DefaultTenantID so the pre-multi-tenant single-tenant
  callers stay correct (and don't accidentally land with tenant_id="").
- Tests covering: tenant_id write isolation, two tenants same provider
  name with composite uniqueness, empty-tenant normalization.

Transport additions:
- handlers.TenantProviderHandler with POST
  /api/tenants/{tenant_id}/providers. Reads tenant_id from
  multitenant.BifrostContextKeyTenantID (set by RequireTenantPathMiddleware
  from patch 0015), validates the payload with the same rules as the
  legacy /api/providers POST, calls AddProviderForTenant, then evicts
  the per-tenant runtime via the new TenantRuntimeEvictor interface.
- BifrostHTTPServer.multitenantManager stashes the Manager created in
  buildInferenceRouter so RegisterAPIRoutes can pass it as the evictor.
  RegisterAPIRoutes mounts the tenant-scoped routes only when the
  manager is non-nil (i.e. BIFROST_MULTI_TENANT_ENABLED is on).
- Tests covering: happy path with eviction, missing tenant ctx, missing
  provider, nil evictor allowed, nil store rejected at construction,
  store error mapping (ErrAlreadyExists -> 409).

Out of scope (follow-on patches):
- GET / PUT / DELETE on /api/tenants/{tenant_id}/providers/{provider}.
- Provider keys CRUD under /api/tenants/{tenant_id}/providers/{provider}/keys.
- Tenant-scoping the legacy /api/providers admin routes for tenant-admin
  callers (requires AdminAuthz to resolve a real tenant from caller
  identity — Phase 4).

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
